{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalShadersQuantization"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Core Inference Components","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoder","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/KVCache","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/PagedKVCache","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/LLMConfig","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/RoPEEmbedding"],"anchor":"Core-Inference-Components"},{"title":"Sampling & Decoding","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/Sampler","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingConfiguration","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/LLMOptions","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies"],"anchor":"Sampling--Decoding"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderInference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftLLM"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Autoregressive Transformer Decoder Inference","role":"collectionGroup"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftLLM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implements modern decoder-only causal transformer architectures (such as Llama 3, Mistral, and Gemma) leveraging MLX unified memory acceleration on Apple Silicon GPUs. Inference is divided into two distinct computational phases:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prompt Prefill Phase ("},{"code":"isPrefill: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Processes all initial prompt tokens in parallel, computing attention matrices and populating the key-value cache across all transformer layers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Incremental Decoding Phase ("},{"code":"isPrefill: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Processes a single token per step, computing query projections and attending over the accumulated key-value history ($O(N)$ attention over cached history, avoiding repeated full-sequence forward passes)."}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"1-Two-Stage-Generation-Loop","type":"heading","text":"1. Two-Stage Generation Loop"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following complete example demonstrates configuring a model, prefilling the KV-cache, and executing an autoregressive generation loop:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import SwiftLLM","import MLX","","\/\/ 1. Initialize configuration and decoder","let config = LLMConfig.llama3_8B","let decoder = TransformerDecoder(config: config)","let cache = KVCache(config: config)","","\/\/ Tokenized prompt sequence","let promptTokens: [Int] = [128000, 791, 7453, 374]","var generatedTokens = promptTokens","let maxNewTokens = 64","","\/\/ 2. Stage 1: Prefill prompt tokens into KV-cache","let promptLogits = try decoder.forward(","    tokens: promptTokens,","    cache: cache,","    isPrefill: true",")","","\/\/ 3. Configure sampling parameters","let sampling = SamplingConfiguration(","    temperature: 0.7,","    topK: 40,","    topP: 0.9,","    repetitionPenalty: 1.1",")","","\/\/ 4. Sample first generated token from prefill logits","var currentToken = Sampler.sample(","    logits: promptLogits,","    config: sampling,","    pastTokens: generatedTokens",")","generatedTokens.append(currentToken)","","\/\/ 5. Stage 2: Incremental single-token decoding loop","for _ in 1..<maxNewTokens {","    \/\/ Forward single token with isPrefill: false","    let stepLogits = try decoder.forward(","        tokens: [currentToken],","        cache: cache,","        isPrefill: false","    )","    ","    \/\/ Sample next token ID","    let nextToken = Sampler.sample(","        logits: stepLogits,","        config: sampling,","        pastTokens: generatedTokens","    )","    ","    generatedTokens.append(nextToken)","    currentToken = nextToken","    ","    \/\/ Check for EOS (End of Sequence) tokens","    if nextToken == 128001 || nextToken == 128009 {","        break","    }","}","","print(\"Generated total sequence: \\(generatedTokens.count) tokens.\")"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"2-Rotary-Position-Embeddings-RoPE-During-Incremental-Decoding","type":"heading","text":"2. Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE) During Incremental Decoding"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"During single-token decoding (","type":"text"},{"code":"isPrefill: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), position frequencies must match the actual sequential position in the generated sequence rather than index ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"RoPEEmbedding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks this via the ","type":"text"},{"code":"positionOffset","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Internal RoPE position calculation:","\/\/ position = positionOffset + tokenIndex","let rotatedQ = rope.apply(x: query, positionOffset: cache.currentLength)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KVCache"},{"text":" dynamically tracks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentLength"},{"text":", positions increment faithfully from the end of the prefill boundary through every subsequent token generation step.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"3-High-Level-Streaming-API","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"3. High-Level Streaming API"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For streaming applications, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LLMModel"},{"type":"text","text":" wraps the decoder and cache lifecycle into an asynchronous sequence:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftLLM","","let options = LLMOptions(","    maxTokens: 128,","    sampling: SamplingConfiguration(temperature: 0.7, topK: 40, topP: 0.9)",")","","for try await token in model.generateStream(prompt: \"Explain rotary embeddings:\", options: options) {","    print(token, terminator: \"\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute two-stage autoregressive generation with full prompt prefill and incremental single-token decoding using Apple Silicon KV-caching."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftllm\/transformerdecoderinference"]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/KVCache":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"KVCache","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KVCache"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KVCache"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/KVCache","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/kvcache","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Key-Value cache storing previous Attention Keys and Values per layer for O(N) generation."}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/RoPEEmbedding":{"abstract":[{"type":"tex